{"agent":"buglane4","data":{"budget":"","claim":"A timeout acquiring the events append lock surfaces to the CLI as a bare builtin TimeoutError, which core.outcome.exit_for maps to None; the CLI re-raises None-mapped exceptions, so the command prints a raw traceback with no clean exit line.","falsifier":"A regression test asserting exit_for(exc) == NOTHING fails against the unfixed code because exit_for returns None.","item":"fix-B-lock-timeout-raw-traceback","mechanism":"_lock._flock catches fsio.LockTimeout and re-raises a bare TimeoutError; exit_for(TimeoutError) is None (not KeyboardInterrupt, no declared exit_code, not ValueError/KeyError), so cli._main re-raises it.","probe":"python -m pytest tests/test_lock_timeout_diagnosis.py::test_a_lock_timeout_maps_to_a_clean_exit_not_a_traceback -x -q","probe_output":"AssertionError: mapped to None, not 2: the CLI re-raises it as a traceback","question":"Why does a CLI command that times out on events.lock print a raw traceback, and does it map to a clean exit code?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e3c6427fd7e276ca02ea2e026","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":190195,"schema":1,"subject":"R5457dfee3f","ts":"2026-11-13T05:12:52.003546Z"}
